35,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"It seems weather and ""comfort"" projects cause the most delays. We must be careful with outdoor work or vague goals.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"I found that general rooms are always full while specialist ones sit empty. Plus, out-of-service rooms cost us a lot in rentals.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,George,,"Our technicians are wasting hours on manual checks that should be automated. Meanwhile, grounds staff are simply missing.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"The data confirms that shared, bookable spaces are the most successful. Also, older blocks are hiding hazardous materials.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Mechanical costs are rising sharply, while surfacing is stable. Also, we have no money set aside to replace old AV kit.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Benjamin, if mechanical costs are rising, that makes the ventilation or AV options quite risky for the budget.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Mizuki, if bookable spaces are the most loved, we should definitely prioritize a general-purpose area.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,George,,"@Shizue, if outdoor work is delayed by weather, maybe we should avoid the path network this year.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@George, that makes sense. But we must also consider the hazardous materials in the old blocks.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,Precisely. Any project in an old block could trigger a budget and schedule nightmare.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Yumi, the rental costs for replacement rooms are worrying. We need a plan that doesn't disrupt the timetable.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Yumi,,Exactly! We need a solution that adds capacity without taking away existing rooms for too long.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,George,,"I'm still thinking about the technicians. If we can automate their routines, it would be a huge relief.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@George, would a ventilation upgrade solve those manual routines?","{""words"":9,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"It might, but @Shizue's point about mechanical costs suggests it would be expensive.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
